"""Independent original-only complete readings, before primary candidate inspection."""
NOTES={
'bukhari:2648':{
'hi':'Read all597 Hindi characters. The prefatory route reaches Urwah, whose supplied account gives the unnamed woman’s theft at the conquest and punishment under the Prophet’s order. A separately explicit Aisha frame then reports repentance, marriage and her later presenting the woman’s needs. Preserve those distinct actual voices and the woman’s anonymity; do not retrospectively make Aisha the explicitly named narrator of Urwah’s earlier clause. The double prefatory route is context, while all actual chronology and actions remain.',
'ur':'Read all538 Urdu characters independently. The own Urwah-framed historical account precedes Aisha’s explicit later testimony about repentance, marriage and intercession for needs. Keep both report components, exact chronology and unnamed woman without importing a fuller name or narrator. Separate the prefatory Ismail/Ibn-Wahb/Yunus/Layth routes only; neither finite body is compiler explanation.'},
'bukhari:2659':{
'hi':'Read all1050 Hindi characters. Two printed routes and alternative narrated-to-me/heard-from-him formulas precede Uqbah’s actual marriage, the nursing woman’s claim, his repeated approach and the final instruction. Keep every finite scene, including the source’s withdrew/separated wording without silently construing it as divorce at that earlier point. The nikah and baqi-reh-sakta parentheses supply the actual object and predicate of the how-question and must remain. The multistep routes and equivalent transmission formulas are context; no missing nursing proof or wife identity is inferred.',
'ur':'Read all938 Urdu characters independently. The double route, Bukhari transition and alternative hearing formula are transmission apparatus. The actual Uqbah marriage/nursing-claim encounter, two approaches and prohibition on retaining Umm Yahya remain. Both parenthetic nikah and baqi-reh-sakta complete the supplied rhetorical question, unlike a lexical label. Preserve the literal intervening juda-ho-gaya action and all exact source names without adding a legal conclusion.'},
'bukhari:2675':{
'hi':'Read all503 Hindi characters. The source’s defective short route and printed Abdullah/Ibn-Abi-Of forms must not be repaired. Its price assertion is repeated and omits Urdu’s explicit contrary claim, so do not describe an unprinted false-price predicate as supplied Hindi. Keep the actual oath/price event, the reported revelation with its actual transliterated verse and supplied Hindi meaning, then the separately attributed Companion comparison. The final कहैं and other defects stay literal; no Urdu-derived खائن repair. Pure route is context, while the actual embedded recitation/meaning are preserved with their role distinguished.',
'ur':'Read all565 Urdu characters independently. The own Ibn-Abi-Awfa report explicitly supplies the false-price oath through its contrary clause, then the reported revelation with Arabic verse and its actual Urdu meaning. Keep both recitation and supplied translation as embedded source content, not an external addition. The final named Companion judgment about deceptive price-raising is separately attributed and is not a Prophet saying or compiler dictionary note. Separate the long prefatory route and preserve every actual condition.'},
'bukhari:2681':{
'hi':'Read all576 Hindi characters. The source relays Abu Sufyan’s report of Heraclius recalling his question and Abu Sufyan’s answer about prayer, truth, chastity, covenant and trust, then Heraclius’s own characterization. Keep that actual reported dialogue under Heraclius/Abu Sufyan, not direct Prophet speech. The Muhammad parenthesis supplies the actual otherwise-pronominal subject and should remain; do not infer an absent identity. Separate the prefatory route, preserving a coherent final relay frame and all five listed traits.',
'ur':'Read all501 Urdu characters independently. The actual source ultimately has Heraclius recalling an earlier question/answer to Abu Sufyan and concluding these are prophetic attributes. Preserve those voices and the exact five-part content, without asserting the closing appraisal as our independent conclusion or as a Prophet utterance. The parenthetic Muhammad supplies the referent of وہ and is material participant scope; the multistep preface remains context.'},
}
